mode: "100644"
text: "# Trend Types & Finding Them\n\nWhat counts as a \"trend,\" how each type is ridden, and where to find them — plus an honest note on\nwhat this skill can and can't do about *discovery*.\n\n## Honest first: this skill vets and executes; it doesn't have a live trend feed\n\nTrends are real-time. What's trending right now changes hourly and can't be recalled from a model's\ntraining data — so **don't trust any AI (including this one) to tell you what's currently trending.**\nThis skill's value is the **judgment (the three gates)** and the **execution (the remix)**. For\n*discovery*, the user brings a specific trend, or scans the live sources below. Treat any \"here's\nwhat's trending\" claim without a live source as unreliable.\n\n## Where to find trends (live sources)\n\n- **Your own FYP / feed** — the fastest read on what's rising in *your* niche. Watch what your\n  audience and peer creators are doing.\n- **Platform trend surfaces** — TikTok's Creative Center / trend tabs, Reels trend tools, YouTube\n  trending, X trending, Pinterest trends. (Re-verify which exist; platforms change them.)\n- **Trending sounds** — the platform's audio library, sorted by what's rising (catch on the way up).\n- **Google Trends** — for search-driven and news-adjacent topics.\n- **Reddit / niche communities** — early signal for memes and topics before they hit the mainstream.\n- **Trend newsletters / creator roundups** — curated weekly trend digests for your vertical.\n- **Real-time tools** — social listening / trend-spotting tools the user may have.\n\nThe edge is being **early in your niche**, which usually means watching your own corner closely, not\nchasing platform-wide mega-trends everyone's already on.\n\n## Types of trends (each ridden differently)\n\n- **Trending sounds/audio** (TikTok, Reels) — use the rising sound under your own content; often the\n  single biggest reach lever on short video. Sync your hook to it. (Mind commercial sound licensing\n  for brand accounts.)\n- **Trending formats / memes / templates** — a repeatable structure (\"expectation vs reality,\"\n  \"tell me X without telling me X,\" a specific edit). Take the *structure*, fill it with your niche.\n  The most brand-friendly type.\n- **Trending topics / hashtags** — a subject everyone's posting about. Add a genuine take; don't just\n  tag in.\n- **News / cultural moments (newsjacking)** — reacting to real events. Highest reach, highest risk —\n  the SAFETY gate matters most here. Light cultural moments (a big game, an awards show, a product\n  launch in your space) are usually fine; serious/sensitive news usually isn't.\n- **Platform features/trends** — a new feature or native behavior the algorithm is pushing; early\n  adoption can earn reach.\n- **Seasonal / predictable** — recurring moments (industry events, seasonal hooks). The one type you\n  *can* plan ahead for — build these into the `content-calendar` instead of reacting.\n\n## Match the type to the gates\n\nSounds and formats usually clear SAFETY easily and live or die on FIT + TIMING. News/cultural\nmoments are the opposite — they can be timely and on-brand but **fail SAFETY** the moment the event\nis serious. Knowing which type you're holding tells you which gate to scrutinize hardest.\n"
